@startuml
title SEQ-16 — Written answer in legacy conversation room
actor Learner
participant "LessonWorkspace" as Room
participant "PrivateLessonText" as Controller
participant "Realtime data channel" as Realtime
participant "GotIt Backend" as Backend

Learner -> Room: Choose text and start lesson
Room -> Backend: Existing owned session request (text mode)
Backend --> Room: Short-lived session credential
note over Room, Realtime: Existing WebRTC connection; no microphone capture in text mode
Learner -> Room: Submit bounded draft
Room -> Controller: submit(text)
Controller -> Realtime: conversation.item.create (stable item ID)
Realtime --> Controller: item.added / item.created (matching ID)
Controller --> Room: Record learner turn once
Controller -> Realtime: response.create (event ID)
alt Tutor response acknowledged
  Realtime --> Controller: response.created
  Controller --> Room: Accepted: clear draft
  Realtime --> Room: Tutor transcript / actual playback events
else Error or acknowledgment timeout
  Controller --> Room: Keep draft; allow retry
  Learner -> Room: Retry same draft
  Room -> Controller: submit(same text)
  note over Controller, Realtime: Reuse accepted item; retry response request only
end
Learner -> Room: Finish and save (confirm)
Room -> Realtime: Existing wrap-up request after current generation
Realtime --> Room: Wrap-up and playback completion
Room -> Backend: Existing complete (actual learner/tutor turns)
Backend --> Room: Actual structured report
Room --> Learner: Summary or report failure/retry
@enduml
